This `useEffect` with an empty dependency array calls `fetchOutstandingReports()`, which triggers an API call (`API.read`). In React Strict Mode, effects with `[]` deps are double-invoked, causing duplicate network requests. Since API calls are non-idempotent side effects (they consume server resources), this needs a guard.

Add a module-level flag to prevent double execution:

```tsx
let didFetchOutstandingReports = false;

// Inside the component:
useEffect(() => {
    if (didFetchOutstandingReports) {
        return;
    }
    didFetchOutstandingReports = true;
    fetchOutstandingReports();
}, []);
```

